#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:57
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:59
msgid ""
"&kappname; is a label designer for Linux. You draw a label on a canvas the "
"size of the real one, with text, addresses, barcodes and 2D codes, pictures, "
"clip art, shapes, counters and dates, and print it on the label printer next "
"to you."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:61
msgid "It supports:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:63
msgid ""
"DYMO LabelWriter printers (the 450 series and older, the 4XL, and the 550 "
"series) and DYMO LabelManager tape printers, through DYMO's own CUPS "
"drivers;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:64
msgid ""
"ZPL label printers, such as the Altec ATP series and Zebra, through the "
"Zebra ZPL driver that comes with CUPS, with labels across the roll and "
"continuous rolls;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:65
msgid ""
"<filename>.label</filename> files, address books (<filename>.ABX</filename>) "
"and Rhino templates (<filename>.rhino</filename>) as DYMO's software writes "
"them;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:66
msgid ""
"printing from data: a label for each row of a CSV file, a spreadsheet or a "
"database query, with questions asked when printing;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:67
msgid ""
"print-only mode for people who only print, an automation service that prints "
"for other programs, and add-ons."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><screenshot><screeninfo>
#: doc/index.docbook:71
msgid "The main window"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><screenshot><mediaobject>
#: doc/index.docbook:73
msgid ""
"<imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"screenshot.png\" "
"format=\"PNG\"/></imageobject>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><screenshot><mediaobject><textobject><phrase>
#: doc/index.docbook:74
msgid ""
"The main window of &kappname;, with the label types on the left and an empty "
"label on the canvas"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><screenshot>
#: doc/index.docbook:71
msgid ""
"<placeholder type=\"screeninfo\" id=\"0\"/> <placeholder "
"type=\"mediaobject\" id=\"1\"/>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:78
msgid ""
"Objects &kappname; does not know are kept in the file and written back "
"unchanged, so a label made elsewhere loses nothing by being opened and saved "
"here."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:83
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:86
msgid "The Main Window"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:88
msgid "The main window has four parts:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:92
msgid "The sidebar"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:93
msgid ""
"On the left, with three tabs. <guilabel>Labels</guilabel> lists the label "
"types of the printer chosen in the print bar; type in the search field to "
"find one, and click a label type to start a label on "
"it. <guilabel>Insert</guilabel> lists the objects to put on a label, and the "
"clip art below them. <guilabel>Address Book</guilabel> holds addresses to "
"print (see <xref linkend=\"address-book\"/>)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:96
msgid "The canvas"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:97
msgid ""
"In the middle: the label at its real proportions, with rulers along the top "
"and left side. The status line under it gives the label's name and size, and "
"the zoom."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:100
msgid "The toolbars"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:101
msgid ""
"At the top: the main toolbar (recently used layouts, new, open, save, undo "
"and print), the insert toolbar, the format toolbar for text, and the arrange "
"toolbar for aligning, grouping, locking and turning objects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:104
msgid "The print bar"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:105
msgid ""
"At the bottom: the printer, what to print, the number of copies and the "
"<guibutton>Print</guibutton> button (see <xref linkend=\"print-bar\"/>)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:111
msgid "Your First Label"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><procedure><step><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:114
msgid ""
"Choose your printer in the print bar. A DYMO printer plugged in over USB is "
"noticed; when it has no printer queue yet, the print bar offers "
"<guibutton>Set Up Printer</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><procedure><step><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:115
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Labels</guilabel> tab, click the label type that is loaded "
"in the printer, such as <guilabel>30252 Address</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><procedure><step><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:116
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Insert</guilabel> tab, double-click "
"<guilabel>Text</guilabel>, or drag it onto the label."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><procedure><step><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:117
msgid ""
"Double-click the text on the label and type. Press &Esc; or click outside "
"the text when you are done."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><procedure><step><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:118
msgid "Press <guibutton>Print</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><procedure><step><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:119
msgid ""
"Save the label with <menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>S</keycap></keycombo></shortcut><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Save</guimenuitem></menuchoice> "
"to print it again later."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:124
msgid "Opening and Saving Labels"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:126
msgid ""
"&kappname; opens <filename>.label</filename> files (die-cut labels and "
"LabelManager tape labels) and DYMO Rhino templates "
"(<filename>.rhino</filename>, which open as tape labels), and saves "
"<filename>.label</filename> files. Labels are saved with DYMO's own label "
"ids, so other label software that reads the file finds the right label."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:128
msgid ""
"Settings that only &kappname; uses, such as a label's data source and its "
"questions, are kept in the file as a comment, which other label software "
"ignores."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:130
msgid ""
"Each time a label is saved over, the version it replaces is "
"kept. "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Versions…</guimenuitem></menuchoice> "
"lists them; restoring one puts it on the canvas, where you save it to keep "
"it, or undo."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:132
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Recently Used Layouts</guilabel>, the first button on the main "
"toolbar, lists the labels you printed last, with a picture of each."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:138
msgid "Designing Labels"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:141
msgid "Objects"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:143
msgid ""
"A label is made of objects. Add one from the <guilabel>Insert</guilabel> tab "
"or the <guimenu>Insert</guimenu> menu, or drag a picture in from "
"&dolphin;. The objects are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:146
msgid "<guilabel>Address</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:147
msgid ""
"A text box for addresses. The checked addresses of the address book print in "
"it, one label each."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:148
msgid "<guilabel>Text</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:149
msgid ""
"A text box. Text can mix fonts, sizes and styles, word by word, print white "
"on black, wrap within its box, and shrink or grow to fit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:150
msgid "<guilabel>Counter</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:151
msgid ""
"A number that counts on with every label printed, with text before and after "
"it, a start value, an increment and leading zeros. A counter can be shared "
"with other computers through a counter file (see <xref "
"linkend=\"shared-counters\"/>)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:152
msgid "<guilabel>Date and Time</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:153
msgid "The date and time of printing, in a format and language of your choice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:154
msgid "<guilabel>Barcode</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:155
msgid ""
"Code 128, Code 39, Codabar, Interleaved 2 of 5, ITF-14, EAN, UPC, QR Code, "
"PDF417, POSTNET, PLANET and Intelligent Mail, and also Data Matrix, Aztec "
"Code, MaxiCode, Micro QR Code, Code 93, Code 11, MSI Plessey, Pharmacode, "
"GS1-128, GS1 Data Matrix, GS1 DataBar, HIBC, KIX (PostNL) and Royal "
"Mail. Other label software that opens the file may not show the types of the "
"second group."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:156
msgid "<guilabel>Image</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:157
msgid ""
"A picture from your files, kept in the label. SVG drawings stay sharp at any "
"size."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:158
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Rectangle</guilabel>, <guilabel>Ellipse</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Horizontal Line</guilabel>, <guilabel>Vertical Line</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:159
msgid "Shapes with an outline and a fill."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:160
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Polygon</guilabel>, <guilabel>Star</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Arrow</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:161
msgid "More shapes. Other label software shows these as pictures."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:162
msgid "<guilabel>Curved Text</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:163
msgid "Text along an arc or around a circle."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:166
msgid ""
"Clip art is in the lower half of the <guilabel>Insert</guilabel> tab: drag "
"an image onto the label or double-click it. Add your own images with the "
"<guibutton>+</guibutton> button. If you own DYMO Label Software, "
"<guilabel>Import / Export</guilabel> imports its clip art from your own copy "
"of <filename>DYMO.DLS.dll</filename>; &kappname; does not include it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:170
msgid "Selecting, Moving and Editing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:172
msgid ""
"Click an object to select it; &Ctrl;-click or &Shift;-click adds objects to "
"the selection, and dragging over the empty label selects every object in the "
"box. <menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>A</keycap></keycombo></shortcut><guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Select "
"All</guimenuitem></menuchoice> selects them all."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:174
msgid ""
"Drag an object to move it and its handles to resize it. The arrow keys move "
"the selection a little, with &Shift; a little more (the steps are set in the "
"settings). Drag the round handle above an object to turn it; with &Shift; "
"held it turns in steps. <keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>[</keycap></keycombo> and <keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>]</keycap></keycombo> turn the selection left "
"and right."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:176
msgid ""
"Double-click a text, an address or a counter to edit its text on the label "
"itself; &Enter; or <keycap>F2</keycap> does the same for the selected "
"object. Double-click another object, or press <keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Alt;&Enter;</keycombo>, to open its properties (see <xref "
"linkend=\"properties\"/>)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:178
msgid ""
"Every change can be undone with <keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Z</keycap></keycombo>. Cut, copy, paste, "
"<guimenuitem>Duplicate Object</guimenuitem> (<keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>D</keycap></keycombo>) and "
"<guimenuitem>Delete Object</guimenuitem> (&Del;) are in the "
"<guimenu>Edit</guimenu> menu and in the menu that opens when you right-click "
"an object."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:182
msgid "Formatting Text"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:184
msgid ""
"The format toolbar and the <guimenu>Format</guimenu> menu change the "
"selected text, or the selected words while you edit it: the font and size, "
"<guimenuitem>Larger Font</guimenuitem> and <guimenuitem>Smaller "
"Font</guimenuitem>, bold, italic, underline and strikeout, and "
"<guimenuitem>White on Black</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:186
msgid ""
"<guisubmenu>Horizontal Alignment</guisubmenu> and <guisubmenu>Vertical "
"Alignment</guisubmenu> place the text in its box. <guisubmenu>Text "
"Fit</guisubmenu> chooses between a fixed font size, shrinking long text to "
"fit, and always fitting the text to the box. <guimenuitem>Wrap "
"Text</guimenuitem> breaks long lines at spaces to fit the box's width."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:190
msgid "Arranging Objects"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:192
msgid ""
"The <guimenu>Layout</guimenu> menu, the arrange toolbar and the right-click "
"menu arrange objects:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:195
msgid "<guisubmenu>Position Object on Label</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:196
msgid "Puts the selection against an edge of the label, or centres it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:197
msgid "<guisubmenu>Align Objects</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:198
msgid ""
"Lines the selected objects up by their edges or centres, or distributes them "
"evenly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:199
msgid "<guimenuitem>Group</guimenuitem> and <guimenuitem>Ungroup</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:200
msgid ""
"A group is selected, moved and turned as one (<keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>G</keycap></keycombo> and <keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>G</keycap></keycombo>)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:201
msgid "<guimenuitem>Lock Position and Size</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:202
msgid "Locked objects cannot be moved or resized by accident."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:203
msgid ""
"<guimenuitem>Bring to Front</guimenuitem> and <guimenuitem>Send to "
"Back</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:204
msgid "Change which object is drawn on top."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:205
msgid "<guimenuitem>Do Not Print</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:206
msgid "The object shows faded while you design and is left out when printing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:207
msgid ""
"<guimenuitem>Layers…</guimenuitem> and <guimenuitem>Move to "
"Layer</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:208
msgid ""
"Objects on a layer show, print and can be edited as the layer says. A layer "
"that does not print suits a picture of the product to design on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:211
msgid ""
"The <guimenu>View</guimenu> menu shows a grid (<keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>'</keycap></keycombo>) and makes objects snap "
"to it (<keycombo "
"action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>'</keycap></keycombo>). Drag a "
"guideline out of a ruler to place objects by; objects snap to it, and "
"dragging it back to the ruler removes it. Hold &Alt; while moving to place "
"an object freely."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:215
msgid "Object Properties"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:217
msgid ""
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Object "
"Properties…</guimenuitem></menuchoice> shows everything about the selected "
"object. The <guilabel>General</guilabel> page has its position and size in "
"millimetres or inches, its rotation and angle, mirroring and a border. The "
"next page depends on the kind of object:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:220
msgid ""
"Text and addresses: the font, the alignment, how the text fits, wrapping, "
"and <guilabel>Grow the box to fit the text</guilabel>, which makes the box "
"wider for longer text, or taller when it wraps, instead of making the text "
"smaller."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:221
msgid ""
"Barcodes: the type, the data, the size and where the human-readable text "
"goes. <guibutton>Build…</guibutton> puts GS1 data together from application "
"identifiers, checking each value and adding a missing check digit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:222
msgid ""
"Images: another picture, how it scales, and a picture file to show instead "
"of the one in the label. The file name may use fields, such as "
"<filename>/photos/{Serial}.png</filename>, for a picture per data row."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:223
msgid ""
"Counters: the text before and after, the start value, the next value, the "
"increment, the minimum number of digits, and a counter file shared with "
"other computers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:224
msgid "Dates: the format, the language, and whether the time is included."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:225
msgid "Curved text: where the text sits on the circle and the start angle."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:228
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>When It Prints</guilabel> page sets a condition: the object "
"prints only when a field is empty, has a value, is or is not a value, "
"contains a value, or is more or less than one. Objects that do not print for "
"the current data show faded. On the same page, an object can stay where it "
"is or stay to the right of a text that grows to fit, moving along with it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:232
msgid "Label Types, Sizes and Rolls"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:234
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Labels</guilabel> tab lists the label types the chosen printer "
"takes. For an Altec ATP printer it lists Altec's labels by product, those "
"fitting the loaded labels "
"first. <menuchoice><guimenu>Layout</guimenu><guimenuitem>Label "
"Type…</guimenuitem></menuchoice> changes the label type of the label on the "
"canvas."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:236
msgid ""
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Layout</guimenu><guimenuitem>Custom Label "
"Size…</guimenuitem></menuchoice> makes a label size that is in no "
"list. Measure one label without the gap to the next. When only part of the "
"label takes print, such as the white strip of a wrap label, give that part "
"too. Your own sizes are listed under <guilabel>My label sizes</guilabel>; "
"right-click one to edit or remove it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:238
msgid ""
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Layout</guimenu><guimenuitem>Roll "
"Layout…</guimenuitem></menuchoice> is for printers that take any label size, "
"such as Altec and Zebra: rolls with several labels across, printed a row at "
"a time, and continuous rolls, where each label takes the length you set."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:240
msgid ""
"<guisubmenu>Label Orientation</guisubmenu> chooses between portrait and "
"landscape. <guimenuitem>Rotate Label</guimenuitem> on the arrange toolbar "
"turns the label a quarter turn together with its objects, so it prints as "
"before."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:244
msgid "Tape Labels"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:246
msgid ""
"LabelManager labels are printed on tape. Objects on a tape label sit in "
"cells side by side along the "
"tape. <menuchoice><guimenu>Layout</guimenu><guimenuitem>Tape "
"Length…</guimenuitem></menuchoice> makes the label as long as its content or "
"a fixed length; <guimenuitem>Move Earlier on the Tape</guimenuitem> and "
"<guimenuitem>Move Later on the Tape</guimenuitem> change the order of the "
"cells. In an object's properties, <guilabel>On the Tape</guilabel> sets how "
"long its cell is."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:250
msgid "Labels of a Kind"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:252
msgid ""
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Label of a "
"Kind…</guimenuitem></menuchoice> makes common labels from a few values:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:255
msgid "<guilabel>Cable Wrap</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:255
msgid "Wraps around a cable and can be read from every side."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:256
msgid "<guilabel>Cable Flag</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:256
msgid "Folds around a cable, with the text on both sides."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:257
msgid "<guilabel>Patch Panel</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:257
msgid ""
"A row of numbered ports at the panel's pitch, with optional arrows and lines "
"between the cells."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:258
msgid "<guilabel>Terminal Block</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:258
msgid "Terminals at their pitch on a DIN rail."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:259
msgid "<guilabel>Breaker Panel</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:259
msgid "Breakers of one module (18 mm) each."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:260
msgid "<guilabel>Rack Markers</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:260
msgid "Height units along a rack's rail, boxed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:267
msgid "Data, Questions and Addresses"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:270
msgid "Printing from Data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:272
msgid ""
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Data</guimenu><guimenuitem>Data "
"Source…</guimenuitem></menuchoice> prints a label for each row of a CSV "
"file, an Excel or OpenDocument spreadsheet, or a database query (SQLite, "
"ODBC for SQL Server and others, MySQL, MariaDB, PostgreSQL, Firebird and "
"Oracle, when Qt has the driver)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:274
msgid ""
"Put fields on the label as <userinput>{Column}</userinput>, in texts, "
"addresses, barcodes or an image's file name; "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Data</guimenu><guimenuitem>Insert "
"Field</guimenuitem></menuchoice> lists them. Each label gets the values of "
"its row."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:276
msgid ""
"<guibutton>Load Rows</guibutton> shows the rows; tick the ones to print. A "
"column can say how many copies each row prints, and another which label file "
"prints it, for a different label per row. All of them must be for the same "
"label type."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:278
msgid ""
"Only queries that read are run (<literal>SELECT</literal>, or "
"<literal>WITH</literal> … <literal>SELECT</literal>), so printing never "
"changes the database. A query can use the answers to the questions, such as "
"<userinput>WHERE Serial = {Serial}</userinput>; they are passed as values, "
"so an answer can never change the query. Database passwords are never saved: "
"they are asked for when printing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:282
msgid "Questions When Printing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:284
msgid ""
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Data</guimenu><guimenuitem>Print-Time "
"Questions…</guimenuitem></menuchoice> sets questions asked each time the "
"label is printed, such as a batch number. The answer fills "
"<userinput>{Name}</userinput> on every label of the print run. A question "
"can be:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:287
msgid ""
"text, with rules: an answer is needed, a length, digits or letters only, or "
"a pattern;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:288
msgid "a drop-down list, of fixed choices or of a column of the data;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:289
msgid "a number, within a range and with decimals;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:290
msgid "a date, in a format of your choice;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><itemizedlist><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:291
msgid "a check box, with the text to print when ticked and when not."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:294
msgid ""
"A text question can be looked up in a column of the data: the row found "
"fills the other questions named after its columns."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:298
msgid "Calculated Fields"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:300
msgid ""
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Data</guimenu><guimenuitem>Calculated "
"Fields…</guimenuitem></menuchoice> works out fields when printing, from "
"other fields, and uses them on the label like "
"columns. <userinput>{Date}</userinput>, <userinput>{Time}</userinput> and "
"<userinput>{Now}</userinput> are the moment of "
"printing. <userinput>{Date+30}</userinput> or "
"<userinput>{Installed+1y}</userinput> moves a date by days, weeks "
"(<literal>w</literal>), months (<literal>m</literal>), years "
"(<literal>y</literal>) or hours (<literal>h</literal>); "
"<userinput>{Serial+1}</userinput> adds to a number."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:302
msgid ""
"After a <literal>|</literal>, a filter changes the value: "
"<literal>upper</literal>, <literal>lower</literal>, <literal>trim</literal>, "
"<literal>left:3</literal>, <literal>right:4</literal>, "
"<literal>mid:2:3</literal>, <literal>pad:6</literal>, "
"<literal>date:dd-MM-yyyy</literal>, <literal>replace:old:new</literal> and "
"<literal>default:text</literal>. For example "
"<userinput>{Date+30|date:dd-MM-yyyy}</userinput> or "
"<userinput>{Prefix}-{Serial|pad:6}</userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:306
msgid "The Address Book"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:308
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Address Book</guilabel> tab holds addresses in a DYMO address "
"book (<filename>.ABX</filename>). Search it, tick the addresses to print, "
"and choose <guilabel>All checked addresses in the address book</guilabel> in "
"the print bar: each prints on its own label, in the label's address "
"object. The <guimenu>Address Book</guimenu> menu makes, opens and saves "
"address books, and imports addresses from a CSV file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:312
msgid "GS1 Data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:314
msgid ""
"For GS1-128, GS1 Data Matrix and GS1 DataBar Expanded barcodes, "
"<guibutton>Build…</guibutton> in the barcode's properties lists the common "
"application identifiers, such as the GTIN, a batch number or an expiry "
"date. Give the values; each is checked, and a check digit left out is "
"added. A value may use fields, such as <userinput>{Batch}</userinput>, which "
"are checked when printing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:320
msgid "Printing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:323
msgid "The Print Bar"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:325
msgid ""
"The print bar at the bottom of the window chooses the printer and says how "
"it is: a stopped queue, jobs waiting, and for a network ZPL printer which "
"labels are loaded and whether it is ready. The button next to the printer "
"opens its settings:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:328
msgid "<guimenuitem>Use as Default Printer</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:328
msgid "Always start with this printer, even when another LabelWriter is plugged in."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:329
msgid "<guimenuitem>Which LabelWriter Is This…</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:329
msgid ""
"For a printer queue that does not use DYMO's driver, such as a printer "
"shared from Windows: labels are then prepared with that model's driver on "
"this computer and sent as they are."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:330
msgid "<guimenuitem>Detect the Loaded Labels Again</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:330
msgid "Asks a network ZPL printer which labels are loaded."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:331
msgid "<guimenuitem>Print Offset…</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:331
msgid ""
"Moves everything this printer prints a little, when labels come out "
"shifted. Print a label, measure how far everything must move, and enter it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:332
msgid "<guimenuitem>Printer Status…</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:332
msgid "How every label printer is."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:335
msgid ""
"Below the printer, <guilabel>Barcodes and graphics quality</guilabel> prints "
"a LabelWriter label slower but sharper. Next to it, choose what to print: "
"only the label on the canvas, every checked address in the address book, or "
"each ticked row of the data source. Set the number of copies and press "
"<guibutton>Print</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:337
msgid ""
"Before printing, &kappname; checks that the label fits the printer: that it "
"is one of the printer's label types, that it is as long as the labels "
"loaded, and that the printer is ready. It asks before printing anyway."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:341
msgid "Setting Up Printers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:343
msgid ""
"&kappname; prints through CUPS. A DYMO LabelWriter or LabelManager needs "
"DYMO's CUPS drivers: the LabelWriter 450 and older and the LabelManagers use "
"<filename>dymo-cups-drivers</filename>, the LabelWriter 550 series DYMO's "
"LW5xx driver. The 550 series reads its status before every label, so it must "
"have a queue of its own with that driver, over USB or the network. A ZPL "
"printer, such as an Altec ATP or a Zebra, uses the <guilabel>Zebra ZPL Label "
"Printer</guilabel> driver that comes with CUPS."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:345
msgid ""
"A DYMO printer plugged in over USB without a queue gets a <guibutton>Set Up "
"Printer</guibutton> button in the print bar; this needs "
"<filename>cups-pk-helper</filename>. Otherwise add the printer in the "
"system's printer settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:349
msgid "Print Settings, Preview and Export"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:351
msgid ""
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Layout</guimenu><guimenuitem>Print "
"Settings…</guimenuitem></menuchoice> sets how the printer prints this label: "
"the DYMO print density, or the darkness and speed of an Altec or Zebra "
"printer. It also sets a header label and a trailer label, printed once "
"before and after a print run and filled with the answers and "
"<userinput>{Count}</userinput>, the number of labels in between."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:353
msgid ""
"<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Print "
"Preview</guimenuitem></menuchoice> shows the pages exactly as the printer "
"receives them, dot for dot, and steps through a run where counters or "
"addresses change."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:355
msgid ""
"<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Export as PDF or "
"Image…</guimenuitem></menuchoice> saves the label as a PDF at its own size "
"or as a PNG image at the printer's resolution, optionally with the label's "
"outline as a proof."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:359
msgid "Counters"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:361
msgid ""
"A counter counts on with every label printed, and its next value is saved in "
"the label. When several computers print the same label, give the counter a "
"counter file on a network share in its properties: the file keeps the next "
"value for every computer, and is locked while one prints, so no number "
"prints twice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:365
msgid "Print History and Printer Status"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:367
msgid ""
"<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Print "
"History…</guimenuitem></menuchoice> lists what was printed, when and on "
"which printer, with the answers and data rows. Search it, open a label as it "
"was printed, or print it again with the same answers and rows."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:369
msgid ""
"<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Printer "
"Status…</guimenuitem></menuchoice> shows every label printer: its queue, the "
"jobs waiting, and what network ZPL printers say about themselves, such as "
"being out of labels or having the head open."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:373
msgid "Print-Only Mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:375
msgid ""
"Print-only mode is for people who only print: "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Print-Only "
"Mode</guimenuitem></menuchoice>, or the <guilabel>Label Printing</guilabel> "
"launcher. Choose a label from a folder, fill in its questions, tick the data "
"rows and print, without being able to change the label. Counters are kept in "
"the label."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:377
msgid ""
"In the settings, an administrator can make the app always start in "
"print-only mode, with no way back to designing, and fix that setting with "
"KDE's Kiosk (see <xref linkend=\"settings\"/>)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:383
msgid "Automation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:385
msgid ""
"The automation service, <command>plasma-label-creator-automation</command>, "
"prints labels for other programs without anyone at the screen, also when "
"&kappname; is closed. It makes the same checks as the "
"<guibutton>Print</guibutton> button: the answers to the label's questions, "
"shared counters, the printer's label types and state. Counters count on in "
"the label, and every print goes in the print history."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:387
msgid ""
"Set it up in <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure "
"&kappname;…</guimenuitem><guilabel>Automation</guilabel></menuchoice>: start "
"it there, or have it start when you log in. <guibutton>Recent "
"Jobs…</guibutton> lists what it printed lately, where each job came from, "
"and why a job was not printed. On a computer without a desktop session, run "
"it as a systemd user service: <userinput><command>systemctl --user enable "
"--now plasma-label-creator-automation</command></userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:390
msgid "Watched Folders"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:392
msgid ""
"Each watched folder has a label, a printer and a number of copies. A CSV "
"file dropped in it prints a label for each row, its first line naming the "
"fields; a JSON file is a print job as sent over HTTP. Printed files move to "
"<filename>printed</filename>, the others to <filename>failed</filename> with "
"the reason in a <filename>.txt</filename> file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:394
msgid ""
"A file is printed once it has not changed for two seconds. A program that "
"writes slowly should write the file under another name, such as "
"<filename>job.csv.part</filename>, and rename it when done."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:398
msgid "Print Requests over HTTP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:400
msgid ""
"When &kappname; is built with Qt HTTP Server, the service also takes print "
"requests over HTTP, from this computer only or from the network. Every "
"request carries the token shown in the settings. Labels are named relative "
"to the labels folder set there, and only labels in it print."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><programlisting>
#: doc/index.docbook:402
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H \"Content-Type: "
"application/json\" \\\n"
"     -d '{\"label\": \"Rack/patch panel\", \"printer\": \"Zebra-ZT230\", "
"\"copies\": 1,\n"
"          \"values\": {\"Port\": \"A12\"},\n"
"          \"rows\": [{\"Serial\": \"S1\"}, {\"Serial\": \"S2\"}]}' \\\n"
"     http://localhost:8631/v1/print"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><sect1><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:408
msgid ""
"<literal>values</literal> fill fields and answer the label's questions on "
"every label; each of <literal>rows</literal> gives one label. <literal>GET "
"/v1/labels</literal> lists the labels with their fields and questions, "
"<literal>GET /v1/printers</literal> the printers and their state, and "
"<literal>GET /v1/status</literal> the service's version and settings."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><title>
#: doc/index.docbook:414
msgid "Configuring &kappname;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:416
msgid ""
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure "
"&kappname;…</guimenuitem></menuchoice> has these pages:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:419
msgid "<guilabel>Designing</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:420
msgid ""
"The font of new text, how far the arrow keys move objects (also with "
"&Shift;), the steps for turning, the tape to start with, and whether the "
"rulers show millimetres or inches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:421
msgid "<guilabel>Printing</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:422
msgid ""
"Whether and how often network label printers are asked how they are, whether "
"to warn before printing when the printer is not ready, the copies to start "
"with, the gap between Altec labels across and the length continuous rolls "
"start at, how long to wait for a shared counter, and print-only mode: the "
"folder its labels come from and whether the app always starts in it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:423
msgid "<guilabel>History</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:424
msgid ""
"How many versions are kept per label, and whether they are kept next to the "
"label in a <filename>.versions</filename> folder, where they go along with "
"the label for everyone who opens it there; how many prints the history "
"keeps; how many recently used layouts are kept."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:425
msgid "<guilabel>Automation</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:426
msgid "The automation service (see <xref linkend=\"automation\"/>)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><variablelist><varlistentry><term>
#: doc/index.docbook:427
msgid "<guilabel>Add-ons</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:428
msgid ""
"The add-ons installed on this computer, each of which can be switched off. A "
"change takes effect when &kappname; starts again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:431
msgid ""
"An administrator can fix settings for everyone with KDE's Kiosk. For "
"example, <literal>LockPrintOnly[$i]=true</literal> in the "
"<literal>[Settings]</literal> group of "
"<filename>plasma-label-creatorrc</filename> keeps people from leaving "
"print-only mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <book><chapter><para>
#: doc/index.docbook:433
msgid ""
"&kappname; speaks the language of your desktop when it has been translated "
"into it; for now, that is English and "
"Dutch. <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure "
"Language…</guimenuitem></menuchoice> chooses another language for &kappname; "
"alone."
msgstr ""

